
This directory contains the source files of WinZ80 version 4.00.
WinZ80 is copyright 1/1/1999 Gerton Lunter.  The source files may
not be distributed or used in other programs.

To compile vz80d.vxd, use the Makefile.  You need MASM version 6,
the include files vmm.inc and debug.inc, and the Microsoft 32 bit
linker.

The files dbgscan.l and asm.l generate lexical analysers for the
monitor/debugger and the assembler, respectively.  Pull these through
flex to yield lexer.c and asm-lex.c.  For convenience, these two
output files have been included.

The source file for asmbison.c (also included) is asm.y.  First,
pre-process this file using e.g. GCC to expand all #define's.  The
result was called asm-pre.y.  Then run bison on this file to get
asmbison.c.

The other files were compiled using Borland C for Windows.  Use the
large memory model, set the Far Data Treshold to a low value to
prevent the automatic data segment from overflowing, and include the
libraries bwcc, import and crtldll.  Assemble the .asm files debug,
wavetbl, emulcb, ddfd, emul, xdcb, inout, core, vid, vid1, vid4,
vid8, vid16, vid24, vid32; the others are include files.


